{"ts":"2026-07-30T06:46:17.635Z","lvl":"debug","ctx":"app:module=llm","msg":"  think","data":{"agent":"main","preview":"The user is saying \"直接报价\" (just give the quote directly), implying they don't want to answer my questions and want me to proceed with what I have. However, the grill_me indicated some missing information. Let me think about this...\n\nThe user clearly wants me to proceed directly with quoting. They're saying \"直接报价\" - meaning they want me to move forward without further questioning. Let me see what I can reasonably assume based on the document:\n\n1. **数据规模** - The document mentions a \"两个月上线计划\" (two-month launch plan) and the project is a startup/初期 project. I can make reasonable assumptions based on typical MVP scale. The document mentions it's a \"一期开发确认版\" (Phase 1 development confirmed version). I'll assume moderate scale.\n\n2. **交付时间** - The document version history shows V6.4 dated 2026-07-26, and mentions \"两个月上线计划\". I can assume 2 months from the document date - around end of September 2026.\n\n3. **品类价格配置** - For 废旧平板, it's reasonable to assume it uses the same percentage as 废旧手机 (default 30%下调) since the document groups them together conceptually as \"废旧\" items.\n\nActually, the user is being very clear - \"直接报价\". They don't want to answer questions. Let me proceed with the process. I'll use reasonable default assumptions and move forward.\n\nLet me proceed with decompose → evaluate → estimate_hours.\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read the context. The user said \"直接报价\" in the first message too, and I asked questions. Now they're repeating \"直接报价\" again. They clearly don't want to answer questions. I should proceed.\n\nLet me start the decomposition."}}
